# Cursor Rules for Form-Flow Project

## Project Context

This is a Form-Flow MCP project - a Next.js 15.3.4 application with advanced form building capabilities using Model Context Protocol (MCP) architecture.

## Key Technologies

- Next.js 15.3.4 with App Router
- React 18+ with TypeScript
- PrimeReact 10.9.6 for UI components
- Tailwind CSS 4 + PrimeFlex for styling
- Model Context Protocol (MCP) for business logic separation

## Project Structure

- `src/app/` - Next.js app router pages
- `src/components/` - React components
- `src/lib/mcp/` - MCP implementations and protocols
- `src/types/` - TypeScript type definitions
- `mcp-curcontext/` - Cursor MCP system for intelligent assistance

## MCP Architecture

The project uses MCPs for:

- FormMCP - Form business logic
- FieldMCP - Field rendering and validation
- ComponentLibraryMCP - Reusable form components
- LayoutSystemMCP - Form layout management
- TemplateLibraryMCP - Pre-built form templates
- FormAssistanceMCP - AI-powered form assistance

## Form Builder Features

- Drag-and-drop form building
- Real-time form preview
- Undo/redo functionality
- Keyboard shortcuts
- Component palette with 25+ field types
- Layout system with 12+ templates
- CSV import/export capabilities

## Development Guidelines

- Use TypeScript for all new code
- Follow MCP patterns for business logic
- Use PrimeReact components for UI
- Implement proper error handling with MCPError objects
- Add comprehensive logging with MCPLogger
- Write tests for new MCP implementations
- Update documentation for new features

## Cursor MCP Integration

The project includes a Cursor MCP system that provides:

- Repository intelligence and navigation
- Component discovery and analysis
- Code generation following project patterns
- Debugging and performance assistance
- Documentation generation

## Code Style

- Use functional components with hooks
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Use proper TypeScript types
- Follow React best practices
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Use consistent naming conventions

## Testing

- Write unit tests for MCPs
- Test component interactions
- Validate form functionality
- Test CSV import/export
- Verify drag-and-drop behavior

## Performance

- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Implement proper loading states
- Optimize bundle size
- Monitor MCP execution times
- Use lazy loading where appropriate
